<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Coronation year earnings/shr up 83 pct.</title>
<headline>Coronation year earnings/shr up 83 pct.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     128	   vs 70</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   56.27	 vs 23.50</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   61.40	 vs 31.50</p>
<p>    Tax			 14.32	 vs 9.42</p>
<p>    Capital employed     626.03	 vs 119.99</p>
<p>    Net asset value/shr (cts) 989     vs 337</p>
<p>Full name:  Coronation Holdings Ltd NOTE - The firm said its securities and benchmark funds management operations had a good year with performance-related fees and the weak rand giving a strong increase in earnings.</p>
<p>Coronation added that in place of a final dividend it is to award capitalisation shares to ordinary and &quot;N&quot; shareholders on the register at November 29. The shares will be distributed in the ratio of 0.5 capitalisation shares for every 100 ordinary or &quot;N&quot; shares held.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
